  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "price-n",
      "cost-n",
      "charge-n",
      "fee-n"
    ],
    "note": "**Price** is the amount of money a seller asks for a thing (*the price of a ticket*). **Cost** is the amount you must spend to get or do something, and is usual for services and totals (*the cost of repairs*). A **charge** is the amount asked for a service or for using something (*a delivery charge*). A **fee** is paid for professional work or to join or enter something (*a doctor's fee*)."
  },
